### Code-Reading Constraints

Never read generated, vendored, or cached trees: `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `vendor/`, `dist/`, `build/`, lock files, and similar. Read source and manifests instead.

## Operating Invariants

- One fact has one maintained home; everywhere else links to it.
- Rule bodies live only in `AGENTS.md` and `aiDoc/`; tool-private directories hold pointers only.
- Changes leave a trace: non-trivial decisions are recorded in `aiDoc/notes/`, and when a decision changes an architecture, contract, or process constraint, the constraint's home doc (`aiDoc/modules/architecture-rules.md`, `aiDoc/contracts/boundary.md`, or this file) is updated in the same change — a note never substitutes for updating the rule itself. Multi-step, risky, or delegated changes are planned in `aiDoc/plans/`.
- Evidence and reporting discipline: run focused checks proportional to the affected surface (never the full suite by reflex; never weaken filters or thresholds to get green). Report results as passed / failed / skipped / unavailable / not-run; an interrupted process is never described as completed.
- Handoffs are complete: exact state, changed files, commands with results, remaining work, blockers, and the next safe action (see `aiDoc/plans/handoff.TEMPLATE.md`).
- Closing double gate: before closing out any change, run the drift self-check — `check_sync.py` when the project-harness skill is installed, otherwise verify affected docs against the `aiDoc/README.md` routing table — and fix any drift in the same change; pitfalls and recurring patterns are captured per `aiDoc/memory/lessons/README.md` (the single source for capture and mechanical-gate rules). Both are part of the Definition of Done.

## Definition of Done

- [ ] Code changes follow the rules in this file and the routed aiDoc child documents
- [ ] Validation commands ran per "Evidence and reporting discipline"; results reported honestly by category
- [ ] Both sides of every changed contract (producer and consumer) are traced and synchronized
- [ ] Changes needing a decision note are written to `aiDoc/notes/`; changes needing a plan are updated in `aiDoc/plans/`
- [ ] Affected aiDoc documents are updated in place (facts refreshed, no appended changelog)
- [ ] Paths and symbol references in docs match the real code
- [ ] Closing double gate passed: the drift self-check (check_sync.py or routing-table review) is green, any drift was fixed in the same change, and pitfalls were captured per lessons discipline

