## When to Regenerate aiDoc

Regenerate or incrementally update the doc system (via the project-harness generate workflow) when:

- Architecture changes materially: layering shifts, top-level directories added/removed, tech stack replaced
- Modules, features, or commands are added/removed so that `aiDoc/modules/`, `aiDoc/examples/`, or `aiDoc/relations/system-map.md` no longer match the code
- `aiDoc/` child docs are added/removed, invalidating the routing table in `aiDoc/README.md` and the quick-routing table above — both must be synchronized even if their own last-updated markers are unchanged
- Routing tables or examples have drifted visibly from the real code

Small changes (a single endpoint or page) need no full regeneration — update only the affected area. After regeneration, verify index and path consistency (every path referenced from `aiDoc/README.md` and the tables above must exist).
